fact WorkItem(id: "WI-626", description: some(value: "scaland: mirror WI-616 semantic-eq dispatch (proposal 051 Phase 2). Rust delivered: Eq.eq/Eq.neq resolver tags SemEq/SemNeq (struct_eq keeps the structural comparator); on ground structurally-distinct operands the builtin reads the operand's carrier sort SHALLOWLY (entity ctor parent / algebra-op parent spec sort) and rewrites the goal to the carrier's OWN short-named eq op from the sort-ops table (Set.eq/Map.eq), resolved as ordinary SLD rules; reflexivity fast-path keeps every current ground answer; neq wraps the dispatch in NAF not(...). stdlib side (shared .anthill files already carry it — scaland only needs the RESOLVER flip + must load the new set.anthill/map.anthill rules): Set provides Eq[T=Set] + eq/subset/member relational rules (element compare = spec Eq.eq, dispatches recursively); Map provides Eq[T=Map] + eq->map_eq delegator + binds/strip_is helpers (delegator exists because is_equation classifies a BODYLESS 2-ary eq-short-named head as an equational law — mirror that gotcha; also mirror the WI-624 nonlinear-head caveat: Map.binds keeps a LINEAR head + <=> output bind). Rust refs: kb/resolve.rs (BuiltinTag::SemEq/SemNeq, BuiltinResult::ReplaceGoal, builtin_sem_eq/builtin_sem_neq/sem_eq_override_goal/shallow_carrier_sort), kb/mod.rs register_standard_builtins, tests/include/wi616_semantic_eq_test.rs. NB scaland has no typer — only grammar/loader/resolver mirror applies."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-626", author: "user", content: "DESIGN CHANGED post-review (mirror THIS, not the first cut): no ReplaceGoal / no NAF wrapper. SemEq/SemNeq share sem_eq_core(positive): (1) reflexivity fast path (structural-equal => verdict); (2) O(1) probe of a LOAD-TIME eq-dispatch index (build_sort_ops_table pass 3: for each sort with a genuine OWN eq per typing::carrier_own_op — parent-gated, body-agnostic — key its entity constructors + SELF-RETURNING ops to the target; Map.get must NOT key Map); (3) hit + both operands DEEP-GROUND => prove <carrier>.eq(a,b) in a CLOSED bounded sub-resolution (fresh SearchStream, SEM_EQ_SUB_DEPTH=100k; first definite proof => verdict; only-residual OR truncated => Delay; exhausted-complete => opposite verdict) — bindings never escape, eq stays semi-deterministic; (4) hit + non-ground => Delay; (5) no hit but an overriding carrier REACHABLE inside an operand (value_reaches_eq_override walk) => Delay (buried some({1,2}) vs some({2,1}) must not decide structurally); (6) else structural verdict. SearchStream gains a truncated flag (set at the depth pop). BuiltinTag::Neq deleted (dead). carrier_own_op extracted in typing.rs; carrier_overrides_eq_family (WI-573 gate) now uses it (body-agnostic) so rules-backed overrides block structural guard refutation. See wi616_semantic_eq_test.rs incl. the 3 soundness-guard tests.", at: "2026-07-03T16:54:07Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-626", author: "user", content: "WI-624 landed rust-side; two notes for the mirror. (1) The 'Map.binds keeps a LINEAR head + <=> output bind' caveat REMAINS CORRECT but its REASON changed: the DeBruijn answer-leak is fixed (WI-624), yet the linear form is still required because a nonlinear head imposes STRUCTURAL identity (discrim synthetic double-bind -> contradiction drop), not unification, on doubly-concrete matches — binds(put(empty,1,some(?x)),1,some(42)) would false-fail nonlinear (WI-633 tracks unification-complete nonlinear heads; map.anthill's NB comment now says this). (2) scaland does NOT need the WI-624 fix pair itself: its withFreshVars already threads answer links through the rename (KnowledgeBase.scala:300-310, the rust legacy-path structure) and it has no DeBruijn/synthetic-vid split — but IF the mirror adopts the rust DeBruijn representation, port the pair: two-pass body_rename-before-links + apply-rename-to-links + occurs-check->contradiction in withFreshVars, AND the fact fast-path gate is_fact && arity==0 in the resolver (plus the WI-624 regression tests: forward-orientation nonlinear head, bodyless and bodied, and the occurs-cycle query).", at: "2026-07-04T19:43:57Z")
